uri">9JQZ</ext-link>, and <ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="https://www.rcsb.org/structure/9JQY" ext-link-type="uri">9JQY</ext-link> and Electron Microscopy Data Bank (EMDB) under accession codes <ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/emdb/EMD-61762" ext-link-type="uri">EMD-61762</ext-link>, <ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/emdb/EMD-61763" ext-link-type="uri">EMD-61763</ext-link>, <ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/emdb/EMD-61744" ext-link-type="uri">EMD-61744</ext-link>, and <ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/emdb/EMD-61743" ext-link-type="uri">EMD-61743</ext-link> for the EP2-PF-04418948 complex, the EP2-TG6-129 complex, the EP4-Grapiprant complex, and the EP4-TG6-129 complex, respectively.</p><p>The source data of this paper are collected in the following database record: <ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biostudies/sourcedata/studies/S-SCDT-10_1038-S44318-025-00611-0" ext-link-type="uri">biostudies:S-SCDT-10_1038-S44318-025-00611-0</ext-link>.</p></sec></sec></body></article>